an centers in the American South. Located in a region historically known for its agricultural prosperity, Orlando emerged during a transformative period of American expansion characterized by the growth of the railroads and tourism. It became a pivotal location due to its strategic position near major transportation routes and the natural beauty of its surrounding lakes and wetlands, which attracted settlers and visitors alike.

